diff --git a/docs/windows-portability.md b/docs/windows-portability.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c2b09de
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/windows-portability.md
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+# Bounded native Windows validation
+
+Version 0.1.1 repairs the existing Windows transport build: preserve Win64
+SOCKET/process HANDLE widths, receive socket data through Winsock rather than
+CRT descriptors, use WSAPoll/InetPton, link ws2_32, pass narrow OpenSSL paths,
+and use binary subprocess pipes. Wire framing and the 65535-byte limit stay
+unchanged. Existing Windows key-permission behavior is not strengthened here.
+
+Configure with MIRRORCPP_BUILD_PORTABILITY_TESTS=ON to run the dependency-free
+loopback framing regression. It exercises a real client send, fragmented reads,
+and partial-line EOF. On the qualification runner, native Windows compile,
+install and this test passed; Linux transport, TLS and registry suites also
+passed. ASCII certificate paths were used. This is not a claim that every
+SDK test, arbitrary Unicode credential path, or Windows ACL policy is qualified.
+
+The Mirrors qualification campaign retains exact source, compiler, OpenSSL,
+SDK prefix, logs and hashes. Rebuild and reobserve them for each candidate.
